                text: "An MCP host normally starts this command and communicates over its standard input and standard output. The bridge opens no network listener, owns no database, and never shells out to the PortReeve CLI. Every daemon-backed tool uses the official JavaScript client over the same private HTTP/JSON Unix socket as other integrations. Diagnostic messages go to standard error; standard output contains MCP frames only.",
